  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 6901.07 Fire watch",
  "priorExpiration": "2021-12-29",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 6901.07 “Fire watch” means the assignment of personnel to an area for the following express purposes:\n\n(a) Notifying the fire department, building occupants, or both, of an emergency;\n\n(b) Preventing the occurrence of a fire;\n\n(c) Extinguishing small fires; or\n\n(d) Protecting the public from fire or other life safety dangers.\n\n(e) The term includes “standby fire personnel”.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at Chapter Heading for Saf-C 6900) #10067, eff 12-29-11, EXPIRED: 12-29-21\n\nNew. #13426, eff 8-3-22",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c6900.html"
